===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|US|informal}} [[self-important|Self-important]], [[pompous]]; [[arrogant]] or [[egotistical]].
#: {{syn|en|bombast|hoity-toity|pretentious}}
#: {{ux|en|It's only a matter of time before some '''highfalutin''' developer builds a huge hotel and ruins the scenery.}}
#: {{ux|en|That one Cajun that moved to Austin is too '''highfalutin''' to come back to Livingston Parish. He's over there with that mean bread lady!}}
#: {{ux|en|His speech was very '''highfalutin'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2015-11-01|author={{w|Hendrik Hertzberg}}|title=That G.O.P. Debate: Two Footnotes|journal={{w|The New Yorker}}|url=https://www.newyorker.com/news/hendrik-hertzberg/marco-rubio-ted-cruz-republican-debate-footnotes|passage=There’s been a spate of stories lately about how Cruz’s rhetoric is more '''hifalutin''' than everybody else’s. He uses lots of big words and dependent clauses.}}

